WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.133
-It is time to settle
some of the biggest

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.834
and most important debates
of all time,

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.000
but I'm gonna need some help.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.567
Season 3 of his show,
"After Life,"

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.534
is available now on Netflix.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:13.434
Please welcome the one,
the only Ricky Gervais!

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.601
Wow, one of my favorites, Ricky!

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:21.200
Ricky, it's nice to see you.
Are you ready to do this?

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.801
-What is it this time?
-Yeah.

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:25.367
You don't like playing the games
on our show as much.

00:00:25.367 --> 00:00:27.634
-The pressure is on, isn't it?
-No, no pressure.

00:00:27.634 --> 00:00:29.234
This game you're gonna love.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:31.968
This one is called
"Ricky Gervais Settles It."

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:33.734
-♪ Ricky Gervais settles ♪

00:00:33.734 --> 00:00:36.868
♪ Ricky Gervais settles it ♪

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:40.267
-So you're the only person
that can play this.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:43.334
We've put your name
in the title of the game.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.701
Yeah.
-Yeah, it's great. I love that.

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:47.601
-Alright, so, here we go.
First up. Ready?

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:51.934
Should you take videos
during concerts?

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:54.868
-No. Just watch the --
You've gone to see someone live.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.234
Watch it live.
-Exactly right.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.067
Good man.

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:03.534
Oh -- oh, my goodness.
Who was the best James Bond?

00:01:05.801 --> 00:01:09.501
-Well, my first thought was
Sean Connery.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.601
-Yeah.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.400
-I don't --
I'm not a big fan of Bond.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.801
I've only watched a couple.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.467
I like Sean Connery
because -- I don't know why.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:17.901
I liked him in "The Rock,"
as well.

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:22.167
Yeah, it's all of that putting
on suits and dry martinis.

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.601
I don't look good in a suit.

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:25.734
I don't aspire to be --
I look -- I look rubbish in

00:01:25.734 --> 00:01:29.601
everything, so, you know,
I'd like him in a tracksuit

00:01:29.601 --> 00:01:32.701
and stained T-shirt
or something.

00:01:32.701 --> 00:01:34.434
-So you can't relate to
James Bond.

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:35.868
You can't relate to James Bond.

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.901
-Yeah, no.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.634
-Next question -- text or call?

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:43.000
-Depends.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.033
-Well, how about,
like, those audio texts?

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:49.167
-No, I can't --
No, because I'll leave it on,

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.334
and then I'll start slagging
the person off.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:54.901
And then they'd just get
a message of me going,

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.934
"Oh, he's a [bleep] idiot."

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:04.067
I'm very nervous about this
and microphones and stuff

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:07.067
that I just --
Text is safe for us folks.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:11.767
-Ricky, what is scarier?
Space or the ocean?

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:14.033
-Well, it depends.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:19.868
If you're in a boat, space would
be a lot scarier, wouldn't it?

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:24.367
Whereas if you're
having a gentle row,

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:28.133
then space
would be really scary.

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:31.667
If you're shooting through space
at 500 miles a second

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:36.734
with no oxygen, then --
I think space, in general,

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:39.968
is a bit scary, because it's --
Yeah, it's, like, you know,

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.100
miles and miles of nothing.

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.767
At least with the ocean,
you think you might

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:48.067
see a lighthouse or
a dolphin might save you,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.367
that like, you only --
You never know.

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.300
Flipper might come along.
-Yes, Flipper.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.334
-But what if
you're waiting for Flipper,

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:57.467
and it goes along and he goes...

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:58.601
[ Clicks tongue ]

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:00.300
And you go, "Brilliant!
Save me."

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:02.434
But you've met
the one mean dolphin.

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.801
You've met, like,
the Charles Manson of dolphins.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:05.934
And he just goes,

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:08.300
"No, you've picked the wrong
dolphin, buddy."

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.801
I think space is scarier.

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:12.901
-Alright, well, not with
those types of dolphins.

00:03:12.901 --> 00:03:16.434
Alright, ready for this?
Who was the best Beatle?

00:03:16.434 --> 00:03:19.534
-Well, I'm gonna say one of
the ones that are alive

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:22.033
in case they're watching.

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:25.033
-Come on.
You can be honest with me.

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:26.367
-Well, Paul McCartney.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:29.434
I saw that documentary,
and he seemed to be

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:32.601
sort of running the show.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:38.601
So, I mean, listen,
they're all great, but --

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.767
Yeah, Paul McCartney
because he did the frog song.

00:03:40.767 --> 00:03:42.567
I like that frog song he did.

00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:45.667
-Yeah, I love that song, too.
Yeah, I like that song.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:49.601
I know exactly -- Alright,
if you had to be a cannibal,

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:50.968
who would you eat?

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:55.434
-Well, I'm vegan,
so it's even worse for me.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.667
-Oh, my God. Oh, my God.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:00.200
-So I wouldn't --
-Why not Paul McCartney?

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.267
He's vegan.

00:04:04.133 --> 00:04:05.267
-Well, it doesn't
make any difference

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:06.701
if you eat someone who's vegan.

00:04:06.701 --> 00:04:08.167
You're still eating meat,
aren't you?

00:04:08.167 --> 00:04:10.734
If you eat a cow,
that doesn't make you vegan

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.067
'cause you're eating
an animal that's vegan.

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.534
-So you wouldn't eat
Paul McCartney

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:14.968
even if you had the chance.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:17.567
-Well, I'd rather not
eat anyone.

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:18.801
I have to say --
-I can't believe it.

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.200
Paul, he's a legend.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.834
He's one of the best -- He's the
best performers of all time.

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.100
-I know that! He's not --

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.767
-You would step over his body --

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:28.067
-That's how you pay tribute to
your heroes, is it?

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.567
You go, "Oh, you're so good.

00:04:29.567 --> 00:04:32.501
You're so good,
I could eat a finger."

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:33.868
Where would you start?

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:37.868
Where would you start
if you had to be --

00:04:37.868 --> 00:04:39.167
That's how I want to go,
I think.

00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:41.868
I just want to be fed
to the lions in London Zoo.

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.467
Just thrown in naked
when I'm dead.

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.200
And then just watch people go,

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.033
"Is that the bloke from
'The Office'?

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:51.267
He's just being eaten by lions."

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:53.901
-Last one, last question.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:56.467
British or American "Office"?

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:02.834
-Well, I thought the British
"Office" was the best,

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:06.334
but my accountant assures me
that it's the American version.

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:09.100
-That's the exact answer.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.434
You heard it here first.
My thanks to Ricky Gervais!

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:12.634
We're talking to Ricky more
after the break.

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:13.634
Stick around.
[ Cheers and applause ]

